Two escapes that lose data and not only markup.

Two backslashes in the source are ONE backslash of text. If the pair does not
come back as a pair, the path loses a level on every write: `C:\\Users` becomes
`C:\Users`, then `C:Users`.

A run of `#` at the END of a heading line is the closing sequence of the
heading, and a reader takes it off. Thus `# Sharp \#` with no backslash reads
back as `Sharp`, and the `#` is gone for good.
